---
// Prerendered to STATIC HTML on purpose (2026-09-10). This page has no
// per-request data — everything on it is hardcoded. Static output is served
// straight from Cloudflare's edge via the ASSETS binding WITHOUT invoking the
// worker, which is what removes the 20s cold start (see CLAUDE.md).
// If this page is ever wired to the CMS, delete this line so it returns to SSR.
export const prerender = true;
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title={'Pricing | Liberty Hearing Center'}
	description={'Published service fees and hearing aid pricing at Liberty Hearing Center in College Station, TX — including what bundled plans already cover.'}
	active="resources"
	footer="pricing"
>
<section style="background:var(--surface-blue)">
<div style="max-width:1280px;margin:0 auto;padding:56px clamp(18px,4vw,32px) clamp(42px,8vw,72px)">
<div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start;gap:22px">
<nav style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;padding:9px 20px;border-radius:999px;background:var(--white);font-size:13px;font-weight:700;box-shadow:0 2px 10px rgba(var(--navy-rgb),.06)">
<a href="/" style="transition:.3s" style-hover="color:var(--gold)">Home</a><span style="color:var(--text-muted)">/</span>
<span style="color:var(--text-muted)">Pricing</span>
</nav>
<h1 style="margin:0;color:var(--navy);font-size:clamp(38px,4.2vw,62px);font-weight:800;line-height:1.06;letter-spacing:-.045em;text-wrap:balance">Pricing</h1>
<p style="margin:0;max-width:780px;font-size:19px;line-height:1.7;text-wrap:pretty">Liberty Hearing Center publishes what each service costs so you can see exactly what you are paying for before you agree to it. The fees below apply to patients who choose the unbundled option or who need a single service on its own. If you purchase hearing aids through us on a bundled plan, the hearing aid services listed here are already included in your plan at no additional charge.</p>
<div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap">
<a href="/book-appointment/" style="display:inline-flex;min-height:50px;align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:12px 24px;border:1px solid transparent;border-radius:999px;background:var(--brand-red);color:var(--white);font-size:14px;font-weight:750;transition:.3s" style-hover="background:var(--navy);transform:translateY(-2px)">Request an Appointment</a>
<a href="tel:9794507996" style="display:inline-flex;min-height:50px;align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:12px 24px;border:1px solid var(--brand-red);border-radius:999px;background:var(--white);color:var(--brand-red);font-size:14px;font-weight:750;transition:.3s" style-hover="border-color:var(--navy);background:var(--navy);color:var(--white);transform:translateY(-2px)">Call 979-450-7996</a>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section style="background:var(--white)">
<div data-stack="2" style="max-width:1280px;margin:0 auto;padding:clamp(42px,8vw,72px) clamp(18px,4vw,32px) clamp(51px,8vw,88px);display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 370px;gap:64px;align-items:start">
<div>
<details open="true" style="margin-bottom:48px;padding:26px 30px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:16px;background:var(--white);box-shadow:0 10px 30px rgba(var(--navy-rgb),.06)">
<summary style="cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;color:var(--navy);font-size:17px;font-weight:750;letter-spacing:-.01em">On this page<span style="flex-shrink:0;display:grid;place-items:center;width:30px;height:30px;border-radius:999px;background:var(--navy);color:var(--white);font-size:16px;font-weight:700;line-height:1">−</span></summary>
<div style="margin-top:18px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px">
<a href="#unbundled" style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;padding:14px 18px;border-radius:10px;background:var(--surface);font-size:14px;font-weight:700;transition:.3s" style-hover="background:var(--surface-blue);color:var(--brand-red)">Unbundled service fees<span style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:13px">01</span></a>
<a href="#outer" style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;padding:14px 18px;border-radius:10px;background:var(--surface);font-size:14px;font-weight:700;transition:.3s" style-hover="background:var(--surface-blue);color:var(--brand-red)">Evaluation of outer ear system<span style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:13px">02</span></a>
<a href="#middle" style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;padding:14px 18px;border-radius:10px;background:var(--surface);font-size:14px;font-weight:700;transition:.3s" style-hover="background:var(--surface-blue);color:var(--brand-red)">Evaluation of middle ear system<span style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:13px">03</span></a>
<a href="#inner" style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;padding:14px 18px;border-radius:10px;background:var(--surface);font-size:14px;font-weight:700;transition:.3s" style-hover="background:var(--surface-blue);color:var(--brand-red)">Evaluation of inner ear system<span style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:13px">04</span></a>
<a href="#aid-services" style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;padding:14px 18px;border-radius:10px;background:var(--surface);font-size:14px;font-weight:700;transition:.3s" style-hover="background:var(--surface-blue);color:var(--brand-red)">Hearing aid services<span style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:13px">05</span></a>
<a href="#aid-pricing" style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;padding:14px 18px;border-radius:10px;background:var(--surface);font-size:14px;font-weight:700;transition:.3s" style-hover="background:var(--surface-blue);color:var(--brand-red)">Hearing aid pricing<span style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:13px">06</span></a>
</div>
</details>

<h2 id="unbundled" style="margin:0 0 10px;scroll-margin-top:150px;color:var(--navy);font-size:clamp(28px,2.5vw,38px);font-weight:800;line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.035em">Unbundled Service Fees</h2>
<div style="width:64px;height:4px;margin-bottom:40px;background:var(--gold);border-radius:999px"></div>

<h3 id="outer" style="margin:0 0 8px;scroll-margin-top:150px;color:var(--navy);font-size:23px;font-weight:750;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-.025em">Evaluation of Outer Ear System</h3>
<p style="margin:0 0 22px;max-width:760px;color:var(--text-body);line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">Checking the ear canal itself, because a physical blockage is one of the simplest causes of hearing trouble and one of the fastest to fix.</p>
<div style="margin-bottom:44px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px">
<details class="pricing-accordion">
<summary class="pricing-accordion-title-bar">
<div class="pricing-accordion-heading">
<strong class="pricing-accordion-title">Otoscopic Exam</strong>
</div>
<div class="pricing-accordion-meta">
<span class="pricing-accordion-price pricing-accordion-price--free">Included</span>
<span class="pricing-accordion-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9.5 12 15.5 18 9.5"></path></svg></span>
</div>
</summary>
<div class="pricing-accordion-content">
<p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">During an otoscopic exam, we look inside the ear canal with a lighted scope. It confirms the canal is clear and the eardrum is intact before any testing begins, and rules out wax, inflammation, or injury as the reason sound is not getting through. This is included at no charge for every patient.</p>
</div>
</details>
</div>

<h3 id="middle" style="margin:0 0 8px;scroll-margin-top:150px;color:var(--navy);font-size:23px;font-weight:750;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-.025em">Evaluation of Middle Ear System</h3>
<p style="margin:0 0 22px;max-width:760px;color:var(--text-body);line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">Testing the eardrum and the small bones behind it, where a cause of hearing loss is treatable and sometimes temporary.</p>
<div style="margin-bottom:44px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px">
<details class="pricing-accordion">
<summary class="pricing-accordion-title-bar">
<div class="pricing-accordion-heading">
<strong class="pricing-accordion-title">Tympanometry and, if required, Acoustic Reflex Testing</strong>
</div>
<div class="pricing-accordion-meta">
<span class="pricing-accordion-price">$50–100</span>
<span class="pricing-accordion-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9.5 12 15.5 18 9.5"></path></svg></span>
</div>
</summary>
<div class="pricing-accordion-content">
<p style="margin:0 0 12px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">Tympanometry measures how well your eardrum moves when air pressure changes, which identifies fluid behind the eardrum, Eustachian tube dysfunction, a perforation, or a problem with the middle ear bones. Acoustic reflex testing adds a second layer of information about the hearing nerve and the brainstem pathway, and helps distinguish between types of hearing loss.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 12px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">Both tests take a few minutes and involve nothing more than a soft probe at the entrance of the ear canal and a gentle puff of air. The price range reflects whether acoustic reflex testing is needed in addition to tympanometry.</p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">Tympanometry alone requires a physician's referral; without one, it must be bundled with a comprehensive hearing evaluation, since insurance won't reimburse tympanometry as a standalone service.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details class="pricing-accordion">
<summary class="pricing-accordion-title-bar">
<div class="pricing-accordion-heading">
<strong class="pricing-accordion-title">Earwax Removal (Cerumen Removal)</strong>
</div>
<div class="pricing-accordion-meta">
<span class="pricing-accordion-price">$125</span>
<span class="pricing-accordion-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9.5 12 15.5 18 9.5"></path></svg></span>
</div>
</summary>
<div class="pricing-accordion-content">
<p style="margin:0 0 12px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">Excess wax is one of the most common and most easily resolved causes of muffled hearing, a plugged or full sensation, and hearing aid whistling. Removal is performed in the office using clinical instruments, after the canal and eardrum have been inspected to determine the safest method for your ears.</p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">This is not a service to attempt at home. Cotton swabs and over-the-counter kits push wax deeper against the eardrum more reliably than they remove it.</p>
</div>
</details>
</div>

<h3 id="inner" style="margin:0 0 8px;scroll-margin-top:150px;color:var(--navy);font-size:23px;font-weight:750;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-.025em">Evaluation of Inner Ear System</h3>
<p style="margin:0 0 22px;max-width:760px;color:var(--text-body);line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">Measuring how much hearing loss is present, in which ear, at which pitches, and where in the auditory system it originates.</p>
<div style="margin-bottom:24px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px">
<details class="pricing-accordion">
<summary class="pricing-accordion-title-bar">
<div class="pricing-accordion-heading">
<strong class="pricing-accordion-title">Visual Reinforcement Audiometry</strong>
<span class="pricing-accordion-note">(ages 3 months to 2.5 years)</span>
</div>
<div class="pricing-accordion-meta">
<span class="pricing-accordion-price">$250</span>
<span class="pricing-accordion-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9.5 12 15.5 18 9.5"></path></svg></span>
</div>
</summary>
<div class="pricing-accordion-content">
<p style="margin:0 0 12px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">A behavioral hearing test built for babies and toddlers. Sound is paired with a lighted or animated toy that rewards a head turn toward the speaker, which lets an audiologist map hearing levels in a child far too young to raise a hand or answer a question. Testing is done at a pace set by the child.</p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">Before we can evaluate the inner ear, we must first rule out any issues with the middle ear. This requires a tympanometry test that is included in the pricing below.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details class="pricing-accordion">
<summary class="pricing-accordion-title-bar">
<div class="pricing-accordion-heading">
<strong class="pricing-accordion-title">Conditioned Play Audiometry</strong>
<span class="pricing-accordion-note">(ages 3 to 5)</span>
</div>
<div class="pricing-accordion-meta">
<span class="pricing-accordion-price">$250</span>
<span class="pricing-accordion-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9.5 12 15.5 18 9.5"></path></svg></span>
</div>
</summary>
<div class="pricing-accordion-content">
<p style="margin:0 0 12px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">Hearing testing run as a game. The child learns to drop a block in a bucket or stack a ring each time a tone comes through the headphones, which holds a preschooler's attention long enough to get reliable, ear-by-ear results across the frequency range.</p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">Before we can evaluate the inner ear, we must first rule out any issues with the middle ear. This requires a tympanometry test that is included in the pricing below.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details class="pricing-accordion">
<summary class="pricing-accordion-title-bar">
<div class="pricing-accordion-heading">
<strong class="pricing-accordion-title">Comprehensive Hearing Evaluation</strong>
<span class="pricing-accordion-note">(age 5 through adult)</span>
</div>
<div class="pricing-accordion-meta">
<span class="pricing-accordion-price">$250</span>
<span class="pricing-accordion-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9.5 12 15.5 18 9.5"></path></svg></span>
</div>
</summary>
<div class="pricing-accordion-content">
<p style="margin:0 0 12px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">The full diagnostic evaluation. It includes a detailed case history, pure tone testing across the frequency range, bone conduction testing to identify where the hearing loss originates, speech testing to measure how clearly you understand words rather than just detect tones, and a plain-language review of your results and what they mean for your daily communication.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 12px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">Speech-in-noise testing is added when indicated, because a busy restaurant or a group conversation is where most people notice a problem first.</p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">Before we can evaluate the inner ear, we must first rule out any issues with the middle ear. This requires a tympanometry test that is included in the pricing below.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details class="pricing-accordion">
<summary class="pricing-accordion-title-bar">
<div class="pricing-accordion-heading">
<strong class="pricing-accordion-title">Cochlear Implant Initial Programming</strong>
</div>
<div class="pricing-accordion-meta">
<span class="pricing-accordion-price">$300</span>
<span class="pricing-accordion-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9.5 12 15.5 18 9.5"></path></svg></span>
</div>
</summary>
<div class="pricing-accordion-content">
<p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">The first activation of a cochlear implant after surgery. Each electrode is individually set to the levels appropriate for your hearing, establishing the map the device will use to convert sound into electrical signals. This appointment is longer and more involved than a follow-up because every parameter is being set from the beginning.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details class="pricing-accordion">
<summary class="pricing-accordion-title-bar">
<div class="pricing-accordion-heading">
<strong class="pricing-accordion-title">Cochlear Implant Subsequent Programming</strong>
</div>
<div class="pricing-accordion-meta">
<span class="pricing-accordion-price">$200</span>
<span class="pricing-accordion-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9.5 12 15.5 18 9.5"></path></svg></span>
</div>
</summary>
<div class="pricing-accordion-content">
<p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">Follow-up mapping visits that refine those settings as your auditory system adapts to the implant. Ongoing adjustment is a normal part of cochlear implant care and directly affects how well the device performs in real listening situations.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details class="pricing-accordion">
<summary class="pricing-accordion-title-bar">
<div class="pricing-accordion-heading">
<strong class="pricing-accordion-title">Tinnitus Assessment</strong>
</div>
<div class="pricing-accordion-meta">
<span class="pricing-accordion-price">$100</span>
<span class="pricing-accordion-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9.5 12 15.5 18 9.5"></path></svg></span>
</div>
</summary>
<div class="pricing-accordion-content">
<p style="margin:0 0 12px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">A standard hearing test measures which tones you can detect. A tinnitus assessment is different — it's a structured evaluation of your tinnitus itself: what it sounds like, how loud or bothersome it feels, when it's worse, how much it masks other sounds, and how it's affecting your sleep, concentration, and quality of life.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 12px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">Tinnitus is subjective, so there's no instrument that measures it directly the same way that an audiometer measures hearing. Instead, we rely on your description, validated questionnaires, and case history to understand the full picture — then recommend in-house counseling and management strategies, or a referral for higher-level evaluation, depending on severity.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 12px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">Those findings shape your management plan: sound therapy, counseling-based approaches, hearing aids with tinnitus features, or a combination.</p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;font-style:italic;text-wrap:pretty">Tinnitus assessment can be purchased alone if the patient has had a hearing evaluation within the past year (either with us or another provider). If not, a comprehensive hearing evaluation ($200) and tympanometry ($50) are required alongside the tinnitus assessment ($100), for a minimum total of $350.</p>
</div>
</details>
</div>
<div style="margin-bottom:56px;padding:24px 30px;border-radius:14px;background:var(--cream);border-left:4px solid var(--gold)">
<p style="margin:0;font-size:16px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">Liberty Hearing Center provides cochlear implant mapping and follow-up care for patients implanted by Brazos Valley ENTs and otologists.</p>
</div>

<h2 id="aid-services" style="margin:0 0 10px;scroll-margin-top:150px;color:var(--navy);font-size:clamp(28px,2.5vw,38px);font-weight:800;line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.035em">Hearing Aid Services</h2>
<div style="width:64px;height:4px;margin-bottom:20px;background:var(--gold);border-radius:999px"></div>
<p style="margin:0 0 26px;max-width:760px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">These services are included at no additional cost for three years when you purchase hearing aids through Liberty Hearing Center on a bundled plan. They are available individually to unbundled patients, and to patients who purchased hearing aids elsewhere.</p>
<div style="margin-bottom:56px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px">
<details class="pricing-accordion">
<summary class="pricing-accordion-title-bar">
<div class="pricing-accordion-heading">
<strong class="pricing-accordion-title">Redux Hearing Aid Drying</strong>
</div>
<div class="pricing-accordion-meta">
<span class="pricing-accordion-price">$50</span>
<span class="pricing-accordion-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9.5 12 15.5 18 9.5"></path></svg></span>
</div>
</summary>
<div class="pricing-accordion-content">
<p style="margin:0 0 12px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">Moisture is one of the leading causes of hearing aid failure, and it accumulates from sweat, humidity, and condensation long before the device stops working outright. The Redux system uses a vacuum-based process to draw moisture out of the internal components in a single in-office visit and reports how much it pulled out.</p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">Patients who live through Brazos Valley summers, work outdoors, or exercise in their devices benefit from this on a regular schedule rather than waiting for a failure.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details class="pricing-accordion pricing-accordion--featured">
<summary class="pricing-accordion-title-bar">
<div class="pricing-accordion-heading">
<strong class="pricing-accordion-title">Redux, Hearing Aid Clean, Check &amp; Programming Adjustment</strong>
</div>
<div class="pricing-accordion-meta">
<span class="pricing-accordion-price pricing-accordion-price--gold">$150</span>
<span class="pricing-accordion-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9.5 12 15.5 18 9.5"></path></svg></span>
</div>
</summary>
<div class="pricing-accordion-content">
<p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">All three services in one appointment: moisture removal, a full cleaning and performance check, and a programming adjustment.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details class="pricing-accordion">
<summary class="pricing-accordion-title-bar">
<div class="pricing-accordion-heading">
<strong class="pricing-accordion-title">Hearing Aid Clean &amp; Check</strong>
</div>
<div class="pricing-accordion-meta">
<span class="pricing-accordion-price">$50</span>
<span class="pricing-accordion-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9.5 12 15.5 18 9.5"></path></svg></span>
</div>
</summary>
<div class="pricing-accordion-content">
<p style="margin:0 0 12px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">A professional cleaning of the receivers, microphone ports, wax guards, and tubing. Daily home cleaning helps, but wax and debris reach places a brush cannot, and a device that has quietly drifted out of spec sounds like worsening hearing to the person wearing it.</p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">Best treated as routine maintenance on a set schedule, not something to book only after the sound gets bad.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details class="pricing-accordion">
<summary class="pricing-accordion-title-bar">
<div class="pricing-accordion-heading">
<strong class="pricing-accordion-title">Real Ear Verification</strong>
</div>
<div class="pricing-accordion-meta">
<span class="pricing-accordion-price">$100</span>
<span class="pricing-accordion-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9.5 12 15.5 18 9.5"></path></svg></span>
</div>
</summary>
<div class="pricing-accordion-content">
<p style="margin:0 0 12px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">A small probe microphone placed in your ear canal measures what the hearing aid is actually delivering to your eardrum using real speech signals. Without it, programming relies on manufacturer averages that account for nothing about the dimensions of your own ear canal. Two patients with identical audiograms and identical devices get different results from ear anatomy alone.</p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">Real-ear verification is the standard of care recommended by the American Academy of Audiology and the American Speech-Language-Hearing Association, and research links verified fittings to better word recognition and higher patient satisfaction.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details class="pricing-accordion">
<summary class="pricing-accordion-title-bar">
<div class="pricing-accordion-heading">
<strong class="pricing-accordion-title">Bluetooth Troubleshooting</strong>
</div>
<div class="pricing-accordion-meta">
<span class="pricing-accordion-price">$50</span>
<span class="pricing-accordion-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9.5 12 15.5 18 9.5"></path></svg></span>
</div>
</summary>
<div class="pricing-accordion-content">
<p style="margin:0 0 12px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">A dedicated appointment to get your phone and your hearing aids working together properly: Bluetooth pairing, the manufacturer's app, streaming calls and audio, hands-free settings, and the volume and program controls on your phone.</p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">Worth booking with a new set of devices, and again any time you switch phones — a new handset can break a pairing that worked fine for years.</p>
</div>
</details>
</div>

